  "notes": "Composed of {嘔|おう} (vomit) + {吐|と} (spit out). A formal/medical term; not typically used in casual conversation.\n\nREGISTER COMPARISON:\n- {嘔吐|おうと}: formal/medical (used in reports, hospital settings)\n- {吐|は}く: standard (\"to throw up\")\n- {戻|もど}す: euphemistic (\"to bring up\")\n- ゲロを{吐|は}く: crude/slang (\"to puke\")\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {嘔吐|おうと}する: to vomit\n- {嘔吐|おうと}が{止|と}まらない: cannot stop vomiting\n- {嘔吐|おうと}{物|ぶつ}: vomit (the substance)\n- {嘔吐|おうと}を{催|もよお}す: to feel the urge to vomit\n\nRELATED SYMPTOMS:\n- {吐|は}き{気|け}: nausea\n- {悪心|おしん}: nausea (medical term)\n- {下痢|げり}: diarrhea (often occurs together)\n\nUSAGE:\nThe kanji {嘔|おう} is complex and rarely handwritten. The word is more commonly seen in print and medical documents.",
